    <text>
    <body>
        
        <div type="letter">
            <div type="text">
                <opener>
                    <placeName>at Hurstbourne Park | Whitchurch</placeName>
                    <date>21<hi rend="superscript">st</hi>. Jany 1868</date>
                </opener>
                <div type="transcription">
                    <p rend="centre">Trout taking for Ova<ref target="#foot.f1"/></p>
                        <table>
                            <row>
                                <cell rend="right">27</cell>
                                <cell rend="centre width30">females</cell>
                                <cell>full &amp; ready to spawn</cell>
                            </row>
                            <row>
                                <cell rend="right">13</cell>
                                <cell rend="centre">do</cell>
                                <cell>spent</cell>
                            </row>
                            <row>
                                <cell rend="right">6</cell>
                                <cell rend="centre">do</cell>
                                <cell>nearly spent</cell>
                            </row>
                            <row>
                                <cell rend="right">16</cell>
                                <cell rend="centre">do</cell>
                                <cell>not ready</cell>
                            </row>
                            <row>
                                <cell rend="right">105</cell>
                                <cell rend="centre">males</cell>
                                <cell>with milt</cell>
                            </row>
                            <row>
                                <cell rend="right">19</cell>
                                <cell rend="centre">do</cell>
                                <cell>spent</cell>
                            </row>
                            <row>
                                <cell rend="right">26</cell>
                                <cell rend="centre">Bright</cell>
                                <cell>in good condition</cell>
                            </row>
                        </table>  
                    <p>Memo: 1 of the males was full of milt though only two years old. 1 female was full of white or very pale eggs.</p>
                    <p>Henry Lee</p> 
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="annotations">
                <note><hi rend="italic">In table</hi>:</note>
                <note>‘16 do not ready’] ‘16’ <hi rend="italic">underl pencil</hi>; ‘62’ <hi rend="italic">added pencil</hi></note>
                <note>‘26 Bright] ‘26’ <hi rend="italic">underl pencil</hi> ‘Males <hi rend="italic">150</hi>’ <hi rend="italic">added below pencil</hi> ‘150’ <hi rend="italic">altered from</hi> ‘140’ <hi rend="italic">red crayon</hi></note>
                <note><hi rend="italic">Top of letter</hi>: ‘Lord Portsmouth’s Park’<ref target="#foot.f2"/> <hi rend="italic">pencil</hi></note>
                <note> 
                    <p><hi rend="italic">End of letter</hi>: <table rend="inlineBlock vAlignMiddle">
                        <row>
                            <cell rend="right">62</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rend="right">150</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell rend="right borderTop">212</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
                </note>
            </div>

            
            
        </div>

        

        

        <div type="footnotes">
            <note xml:id="foot.f1">CD summarised the information in this table in <ref target="../bibliographies/bibl_1966.xml" resp="#mjhawkins"><hi rend="italic">Descent</hi></ref> 1: 308: ‘Mr. H. Lee informs me that out of 212 trout … in Lord Portsmouth’s park, 150 were males and 62 females’. The information appears in a general discussion of the proportion of the sexes in animals (<ref target="../bibliographies/bibl_1966.xml" resp="#mjhawkins"><hi rend="italic">Descent</hi></ref> 1: 300–15).</note>
            <note xml:id="foot.f2">Hurstbourne Park, near the village of Hurstbourne Priors in Hampshire, was the seat of the earl of Portsmouth (<ref target="../bibliographies/bibl_5798.xml" resp="#mjhawkins"><hi rend="italic">National gazetteer of Great Britain and Ireland</hi></ref> 1868).</note>
        </div>        
            
    </body>
    </text>
